# `apps/{{id}}/`: {{name}} as an Orivon app

**What lives here.** A recipe, a manifest, and the bridge that stands in for the Electron main
process {{name}} expects. **No {{name}} source and no {{name}} build output is in this
repository** -- see [`UPSTREAM.md`](UPSTREAM.md) for its licence and where it goes instead.

| File | What it is |
|---|---|
| [`recipe.json`](recipe.json) | Where upstream is, at which commit, and how to build it |
| [`orivon.json`](orivon.json) | The manifest -- what the consent dialog shows a person |
| [`bridge/{{id}}.js`](bridge/{{id}}.js) | `window.{{bridgeName}}`, rebuilt over `orivon.*` |

## Running it

```bash
orivon-port run {{id}}
```

Then open `http://127.0.0.1:{{port}}` in Orivon and accept the prompt -- or `{{eth}}`, once
`orivon-port names` has written `out/names.json` and Orivon was started with
`ORIVON_ETH_NAMES_FILE` pointing at it.

